--TEST--
`Core\Passkey::credentialId` of a request body returns `tainted bytes`, so a plain `bytes` variable does not accept it — `rule:core-classes/passkey-verifies-a-webauthn-ceremony` and `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Passkey::credentialId
// The id is what the browser claims. Nothing has checked it yet, so it stays `tainted`.
bytes $id = Core\Passkey::credentialId(Core\Request::body());
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `bytes`, found `tainted bytes`
  --> case.nvs:4:13
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
